  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your Jokers! They are your best chance to complete a long sequence. However, if you see an opponent has only 2 cards left, discard your Joker immediately to avoid the 50-point penalty. Prioritize forming sequences over setsâ€”they're harder for opponents to block.\n\nOpening Strategy: Don't 'open' (lay down cards) as soon as you hit the minimum if you have cards that could be easily played off by others. Wait until you can lay down most of your hand at once. Watch the discard pileâ€”if the player to your left keeps taking your discards, stop feeding them cards they need.\n\nDiscard Control: Pay attention to what the person to your left is picking up from the discard pile. If they pick up a 7 of Spades, they are likely building a 'Seven' set or a Spades sequenceâ€”do not feed them Spades! The 'Loba' play: Sometimes hold a complete meld in hand to surprise opponents, going out unexpectedly when they think they have time.",
    Player: "Keep your Jokers! They are your best chance to complete a long sequence. However, if you see an opponent has only 2 cards left, discard your Joker immediately to avoid the 50-point penalty. Prioritize forming sequences over setsâ€”they're harder for opponents to block.\n\nOpening Strategy: Don't 'open' (lay down cards) as soon as you hit the minimum if you have cards that could be easily played off by others. Wait until you can lay down most of your hand at once. Watch the discard pileâ€”if the player to your left keeps taking your discards, stop feeding them cards they need.\n\nDiscard Control: Pay attention to what the person to your left is picking up from the discard pile. If they pick up a 7 of Spades, they are likely building a 'Seven' set or a Spades sequenceâ€”do not feed them Spades! The 'Loba' play: Sometimes hold a complete meld in hand to surprise opponents, going out unexpectedly when they think they have time.",
